## temporary workaround

For wheel users, I made [a release](https://github.com/huawei-csl/PTOAS/releases/tag/20260214.post1) prior to the last commit

## Problem

Most [PTO-ISA cpp examples](https://gitcode.com/cann/pto-isa/blob/699931c6400b68bd19e3803eec61ad0268e2aeb0/demos/torch_jit/add/add_custom.cpp#L35-L36) resets vector mask in the beginning:

```cpp
set_mask_norm();
set_vector_mask(-1, -1);
```

But ptoas-generated cpp does **not** reset vector mask. If the previous kernel modifies vector mask, then the current kernel might hit **indeterministic run-time error**, usually `VEC instruction error: the ub address out of bounds`

## Reproduce

For example, if I insert these two lines

```cpp
  set_mask_count();
  set_vector_mask(0, 128);
```

into this ptoas-generated example:

