The error msg `VEC instruction error: the ub address out of bounds` is due to the modified vector mask. Such error can also be caused by a previous kernel call, modifying the mask unexpectedly.

## Suggested Solution

If always resetting `set_mask_norm(); set_vector_mask(-1, -1);` in the generated cpp, then the error can be avoided, regardless of previous mask status. `pto.SectionVectorOp()` regions can by default resetting the mask.

(notice that tilelang-ascend also [always generate these two lines](https://github.com/tile-ai/tilelang-ascend/blob/96c01413021dedc7b3a6648a4efba9dc365bcca1/src/target/codegen_ascend_pto.cc#L2155-L2161)!)

